 "honest": [
  "Cells are a cross-section on the SAME timeline, so unlike E196's eras they cannot be made disjoint: the pooled p treats correlated members as separate evidence and is quoted beside the per-cell count that the rule also requires.",
  "The measured quantity is a single ETF's monthly return versus the benchmark, not the family's book-versus-benchmark level gap, so a window effect here is a mechanism for relative performance and still does not license the drop family's era verdicts.",
  "The basket is 20 declared names with local files; a name without a file is published in missing_files and is NOT replaced, so the panel is whatever those names are, not a random sample of the ETF universe.",
  "The final month is dropped wherever the benchmark file ends mid-month, because a partial month is not a monthly return."
 ],
